+      "description": "The IMPORTED-EVIDENCE per-requirement outcome vocabulary, owned by imported-evidence.schema.json#/x-opensip-imported-requirement-law. It applies to a repair EvidenceRequirement whose relation is `runtime-observation` or `history-change` - relations that mint no fact2, carry no sourceUniverse/targetUniverse and have no Coverage entry, so native section 4.6 `sufficiency_v2` cannot produce an outcome for them and is not asked to. Every member is bound to the payload field that grounds it, and EACH KIND REPORTS ONLY ITS OWN: a runtime requirement is projected through observability, observationWindow and observedPopulation; a history requirement through revisionRange and collectionScope, which are its BOUNDS fields - HistoryPayloadV1 has others, notably its subjects, but it carries no observationWindow, observedPopulation or observability at all. A satisfied imported requirement means the condition was met over the BOUND window or range - not that the evidence is positive: `observed-hit` is positive execution evidence and `observable-unhit` is bounded NEGATIVE evidence, and the disclosure records which satisfied it. No imported observation establishes a universal negative, and imported evidence can never BY ITSELF establish the native closed world or authorize an unsafe delete or replace - though it may be an additional required condition alongside an already-established native basis.",
